add('TCritDesign', 'critic', ['operability', 'C1', 'design'], 'design alternative attack', f"""
Item C1-R3. Attack the DESIGN: the fix keeps the caller's spaced TMPDIR by aliasing it through /proc/self/fd. Alternatives: (i) a whitespace-free symlink created inside TMPDIR (a write outside the fixture tree, racy), (ii) failing fast with an explicit message when TMPDIR has refused characters (the round-47 spot-check also permitted 'fail safe'), (iii) `cd "$TMPDIR"` and a relative base, (iv) making root_locator_class accept the alias form only. Which is the least-surprising, and does the chosen design widen the census's trust surface (the fixture roots handed to the census as caller root overrides are classified by `root_locator_class`; does `/proc/self/fd/24x/...` classify `absolute` for the right reason — read the function, `git -C {L} show {FREEZE}:{CEN}`)? Is the /proc dependency acceptable on this host class? Verdict with the strongest argument for and against; propose exact changes only if you find a real defect.""")
add('TCritClaim', 'critic', ['operability', 'C1', 'do-nothing'], 'do-nothing reachability attack', f"""
Item C1-R4. Attack claim C1 and its counter as a CHEAT: build the cheapest census mutants that satisfy the frozen predicate WITHOUT doing the claimed work, and run each through `python3 {L}/{C1C} --census <mutant> --work {SC}/TCritClaim/w<k>` (one at a time, 5-10 min each; at most 4 runs): e.g. (1) base blob with the case count patched to print 166 and the usage text edited, (2) the fix with `selftest_base_dir` returning the real path without alias but the fixture still built in /tmp and logged through a decoy mktemp call, (3) a census whose `--selftest` forks the real work under a private PATH so the wrapper never sees the creation (the counter would then log 0 creations: loc fails — confirm), (4) a trap that exits 143 but leaves the fixture. Which cheats pass? Each pass is a defect of the counter (report the exact mutant bytes and the leg that should have caught it). Also state whether any predicate clause is a universal that the counter does not enumerate.""")
